WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How are you?
-Good.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.670
-It´s always nice to see you.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.505
Your show is very unlike --
there are a lot of travel shows.

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.941
There´s a lot of shows where
people eat food on the road.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.377 size:88% position:44%
Yours is very different,
because you are not --

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.312
You rarely talk with people
who are selling anything.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re not dealing
with tourist agencies.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:17.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it must be difficult
to find your way to the places

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
that tour guides
don´t want to show you.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:23.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we try really hard
to get that right.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.357
We´ve learned a lot of lessons,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of them painfully
over the years.

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, your local contacts
on the ground,

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
they have to know the area.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have to have
a sense of humor.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
They have to know
what you´re not looking for.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.102
You know, we´re not looking
to do top-ten best lists

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
or a fair
and comprehensive overview.

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
some of the places that we go,

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have a bad fixer,
you´re really in trouble.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
We learned --

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.715
Like, in Sicily, we had
a problematic fixer once.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.383
And, you know, he promised,

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.286
"I´m going to take you to the
best pizzeria in all of Sicily,

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, by the way,
my brother owns."

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:58.925 size:84% position:42%
You know? So it´s not
what we´re looking for.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:00.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Exactly.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.595 size:84% position:42%
How quickly do you know
you have a dud fixer?

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh...pretty quickly.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:10.036
-You know, I think -- I´m not
going to say which country.

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
We went to one country
with a New Yorker

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
who claimed to have
deep roots in this area.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
Had spent, you know,
many years there, he said.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:21.014
And we showed up with him, and
all the locals immediately --

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they´re talking to me
and saying --

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could hear them say,
"Who is this jerk?"

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:27.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.022
-You have -- I don´t know

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:31.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
if it was the fixer´s fault,
if it was your fault,

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.425
if this was just a core fault

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the governments
that are mad at you.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:36.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have run afoul
of some foreign governments.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, I have.
You know, those --

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.168 size:84% position:42%
The worst-case scenario
is when the government

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:45.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of tries to infiltrate
your local crew

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:48.508 size:88% position:44%
and make things prettier
than they are, you know?

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:51.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you know,
official bodies enter,

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we´re shooting with
a butcher in rural Romania.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.616
You know, we like to do typical
things with typical people.

00:01:56.616 --> 00:01:59.686
And we had a local butcher
in a rural area of Romania,

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.121
set to go with his family.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
Apparently
the government found out.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
They arrived the night before,
unbeknownst to us.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.927
It´s like, "You know, your house
is not attractive enough.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:11.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
We move you to nicer house.
Dress your children."

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:14.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, an 8-year-old
and his 9-year-old sister.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.802
"Dress them in traditional garb!

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
Make them dance
for the Americans!"

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it´s just this
painfully false, awkward --

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.308
These terrified children dancing

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
like little humble
figurines, you know?

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember that episode
and thinking,

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:29.516
"I don´t know if girls dance
at Romanian butchers, but..."

00:02:29.516 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Do not shoot stray dogs.
Do not shoot gypsy.

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:36.523
Only shoot, you know, nice, new
Hilton Hotel, Cadillac."

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.725
-That´s good. When you said,
"Do not shoot stray dogs,"

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.160
I thought a different thing.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.028
-No, that would be okay.
-I forgot you have cameras.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
I forgot you have cameras.
I was like, "No, I don´t know.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
That seems pretty
forward-thinking of the
Romanian government."

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A big scandal.

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, of course, by trying
to manipulate reality,

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:55.041
you know, it ended up being
a very tragically funny show.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was all over
the newspapers in Romania

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a KGB agent, Mossad agent,
then CIA agent.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
All at the same time.
-So probably not going back.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Never say never.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you´re a Mossad agent,
you´ll find your way back in.

